{"tag":"section","attrib":{"id":"id6b3c5589-86b3-11f1-8c1e-ca5e0ea6b57b","identifier":"/us/usc/t15/s1054"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"num","attrib":{"value":"1054"},"text":"§ 1054.","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":" Collective marks and certification marks registrable","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"content","attrib":{},"text":"\n","children":[{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"Subject to the provisions relating to the registration of trademarks, so far as they are applicable, collective and certification marks, including indications of regional origin, shall be registrable under this chapter, in the same manner and with the same effect as are trademarks, by persons, and nations, States, municipalities, and the like, exercising legitimate control over the use of the marks sought to be registered, even though not possessing an industrial or commercial establishment, and when registered they shall be entitled to the protection provided in this chapter in the case of trademarks, except in the case of certification marks when used so as to represent falsely that the owner or a user thereof makes or sells the goods or performs the services on or in connection with which such mark is used. Applications and procedure under this section shall conform as nearly as practicable to those prescribed for the registration of trademarks.","children":[],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":null},{"tag":"sourceCredit","attrib":{"id":"id6b3c558a-86b3-11f1-8c1e-ca5e0ea6b57b"},"text":"(","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/act/1946-07-05/ch540"},"text":"July 5, 1946, ch. 540","children":[],"tail":", title I, § 4, "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/60/429"},"text":"60 Stat. 429","children":[],"tail":"; "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/100/667/tI/s106"},"text":"Pub. L. 100–667, title I, § 106","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"date","attrib":{"date":"1988-11-16"},"text":"Nov. 16, 1988","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/102/3938"},"text":"102 Stat. 3938","children":[],"tail":"; "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/106/43/s6/b"},"text":"Pub. L. 106–43, § 6(b)","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"date","attrib":{"date":"1999-08-05"},"text":"Aug. 5, 1999","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/113/220"},"text":"113 Stat. 220","children":[],"tail":".)"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"notes","attrib":{"type":"uscNote","id":"id6b3c558b-86b3-11f1-8c1e-ca5e0ea6b57b"},"text":"\n","children":[{"tag":"note","attrib":{"role":"crossHeading","topic":"editorialNotes","id":"id6b3c558c-86b3-11f1-8c1e-ca5e0ea6b57b"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"b","attrib":{},"text":"Editorial Notes","children":[],"tail":null}],"tail":null}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"note","attrib":{"topic":"priorProvisions","id":"id6b3c558d-86b3-11f1-8c1e-ca5e0ea6b57b"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":"Prior Provisions","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"Acts ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/act/1905-02-20/ch592/s1"},"text":"Feb. 20, 1905, ch. 592, § 1","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/33/724"},"text":"33 Stat. 724","children":[],"tail":"; "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/act/1906-05-04/ch2081/s1"},"text":"May 4, 1906, ch. 2081, § 1","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/34/168"},"text":"34 Stat. 168","children":[],"tail":"; "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/act/1909-02-18/ch144"},"text":"Feb. 18, 1909, ch. 144","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/35/628"},"text":"35 Stat. 628","children":[],"tail":"; "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/act/1930-04-11/ch132/s4"},"text":"Apr. 11, 1930, ch. 132, § 4","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/46/155"},"text":"46 Stat. 155","children":[],"tail":"; "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/act/1938-06-10/ch332/s1"},"text":"June 10, 1938, ch. 332, § 1","children":[],"tail":", "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/52/638"},"text":"52 Stat. 638","children":[],"tail":"."}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"note","attrib":{"topic":"amendments","id":"id6b3c558e-86b3-11f1-8c1e-ca5e0ea6b57b"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":"Amendments","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"1999—","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/106/43"},"text":"Pub. L. 106–43","children":[],"tail":" substituted “trademarks” for “trade-marks” wherever appearing."}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"1988—","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/100/667"},"text":"Pub. L. 100–667","children":[],"tail":" substituted “origin,” for “origin used in commerce,” and “except in the case of certification marks when” for “except when” and struck out after first sentence “The Commissioner may establish a separate register for such collective marks and certification marks.”"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"note","attrib":{"role":"crossHeading","topic":"statutoryNotes","id":"id6b3c558f-86b3-11f1-8c1e-ca5e0ea6b57b"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"b","attrib":{},"text":"Statutory Notes and Related Subsidiaries","children":[],"tail":null}],"tail":null}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"note","attrib":{"topic":"effectiveDateOfAmendment","id":"id6b3c5590-86b3-11f1-8c1e-ca5e0ea6b57b"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":"Effective Date of 1988 Amendment","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"Amendment by ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/100/667"},"text":"Pub. L. 100–667","children":[],"tail":" effective one year after "},{"tag":"date","attrib":{"date":"1988-11-16"},"text":"Nov. 16, 1988","children":[],"tail":", see "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/pl/100/667/s136"},"text":"section 136 of Pub. L. 100–667","children":[],"tail":", set out as a note under "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/usc/t15/s1051"},"text":"section 1051 of this title","children":[],"tail":"."}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"note","attrib":{"topic":"miscellaneous","id":"id6b3c5591-86b3-11f1-8c1e-ca5e0ea6b57b"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":"Repeal and Effect on Existing Rights","children":[],"tail":null},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"Repeal of inconsistent provisions, effect of this chapter on pending proceedings and existing registrations and rights under prior acts, see notes set out under ","children":[{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/usc/t15/s1051"},"text":"section 1051 of this title","children":[],"tail":"."}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"note","attrib":{"role":"crossHeading","topic":"execDoc","id":"id6b3c5592-86b3-11f1-8c1e-ca5e0ea6b57b"},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":null,"children":[{"tag":"b","attrib":{},"text":"Executive Documents","children":[],"tail":null}],"tail":null}],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"note","attrib":{"topic":"transferOfFunctions","id":"id6b3c5593-86b3-11f1-8c1e-ca5e0ea6b57b"},"text":"\n","children":[{"tag":"heading","attrib":{},"text":"Transfer of Functions","children":[],"tail":"\n"},{"tag":"p","attrib":{},"text":"For transfer of functions of other officers, employees, and agencies of Department of Commerce, with certain exceptions, to Secretary of Commerce, with power to delegate, see Reorg. Plan No. 5 of 1950, §§ 1, 2, eff. ","children":[{"tag":"date","attrib":{"date":"1950-05-24"},"text":"May 24, 1950","children":[],"tail":", 15 F.R. 3174, "},{"tag":"ref","attrib":{"href":"/us/stat/64/1263"},"text":"64 Stat. 1263","children":[],"tail":", set out in the Appendix to Title 5, Government Organization and Employees."}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":"\n"}],"tail":null}
